    "title": "Charlotte 49ers game vs. Memphis moved to Saturday morning - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Doug Coats ,\n2 hours ago\nCHARLOTTE, N.C. (CAROLINA SPORTS LIVE) -- The Charlotte 49ers football game against Memphis on Saturday will kick off earlier than scheduled.\nThe team announced Thursday that the American Conference matchup is set to begin at 11 a.m. instead of 3:30 p.m., due to expected showers and storms. The game also is Homecoming for the 49ers.\nMemphis is 3-1, coming off of a 45-21 win over Tennessee-Martin. Meanwhile, Charlotte (0-4) is still looking for its first win since last September.\nThe game will still be available on ESPN+.\nGameday parking will open at 8 a.m.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Queen City News.",
